-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the record, sixteen texts at a time
-- The source's modules in sixteen packs, by the first digit of each module's name (its content's hash):
-- a pack is its modules' texts one after another, a newline after each (P.text), its modules' names
-- beside it (P.mods). A query reads one pack at a time. A pack is written again when its modules are not
-- the ones it was written from; whether any is, is asked only when the index's directory of modules has
-- changed (its time, to the nanosecond, kept in the stamp). A pack is written piece by piece, each piece's
-- bytes passed to the file as they were read.
c-dir : List Word
c-dir = "build/chat/p/"
